tolome-base (0.4.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Login screen avatar: GDM reads /var/lib/AccountsService/icons/<user>, not
    ~/.face, so it showed the generic icon. New /usr/lib/tolome/set-avatar
    gives the Tɔlɔmɛ baobab (/usr/share/tolome/face.png) to ordinary accounts
    as their AccountsService icon. A picture chosen by the user is never
    overwritten: an existing Icon= key (except the default ~/.face, which GDM
    cannot read), an existing icons/<user> file or a personal ~/.face are left
    alone.
  * tolome-avatar.service runs it at boot, before accounts-daemon and the
    display manager (accounts created by Calamares get the baobab at the first
    login screen); tolome-avatar.path runs it whenever /etc/passwd changes
    (adduser, useradd, Settings).
  * prerm: remove the icons installed by the package (user pictures kept).
  * Tests: tests/test-set-avatar.sh (including the .path chain with systemd).

 -- Anhky <dev@tolome.net>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0100

